Suggests: cage, weston, ffmpeg, orca, system-config-printer, at-spi2-core
Description: Debian Minerva desktop environment (Rust core, real X11 session)
 Minerva is a real desktop environment for Debian. A dependency-free Rust
 session daemon owns session state and the system layer: it launches real
 applications (parsed from the installed .desktop catalogue), opens shell
 panels as real X windows, and controls the actual system — volume (pactl),
 Wi-Fi (nmcli), resolution (xrandr), brightness, night light and power.
 .
 Installing this package adds a "Minerva" entry to the display manager
 (GDM, LightDM, SDDM). The session runs Openbox as window manager plus ONE
 fullscreen Minerva shell surface (wallpaper, top bar, taskbar dock,
 launcher, popovers, notifications, settings) while real applications run
 as ordinary X clients on top — listed, focused and closed from the dock
 through the EWMH client list. Background services (notification daemon,
 clipboard, polkit agent) autostart like on any standard desktop.
 .
 Also includes: light/dark theming with 6 accents and 5 wallpapers, a
 Rust-backed terminal, notification shade and real apt package search and
 install. No Google services or branding.
